.TH REPROXY 1 "2026-10-13" "reProxy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reproxy \- intercepting proxy for inspecting, editing and replaying HTTP traffic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B reproxy
[\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B reProxy
runs a local proxy that records the HTTP traffic passing through it,
and a desktop window for inspecting that traffic, holding requests and
responses for editing, and replaying them.
.PP
Point a browser's proxy at 127.0.0.1 on the configured port
(7193 by default). SOCKS5, SOCKS4, SOCKS4a, HTTP and HTTPS proxying are all
served on that one port. To read HTTPS, install reProxy's CA certificate into the
browser from Settings.
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.BI \-port " n"
Proxy listen port for this session. The default is the saved setting,
initially 7193. If the port is in use, the next free one above it is taken.
.TP
.BI \-config " path"
Path to the settings file. The default is
.IR ~/.reproxy/config.json .
.TP
.B \-headless
Run without the window: the proxy, the group hub and the MCP server only.
This is what the
.B reproxy\-mcp
service runs. The process runs until it is interrupted or terminated.
.TP
.B \-verbose
Log connection-level detail to standard error.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH MCP SERVER
reProxy serves its tools to MCP clients over HTTP on 127.0.0.1:3917 by
default, at the
.I /mcp
path, behind a bearer token kept in
.IR ~/.reproxy/secrets.json .
The server runs inside whichever reProxy process currently holds the hub
role, so it is available whenever at least one process is running.
.PP
To keep it available with no window open, enable the per-user service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now reproxy\-mcp
.fi
.RE
.PP
On macOS the same service is a LaunchAgent, installed from inside the
application bundle:
.PP
.RS
.nf
/Applications/reProxy.app/Contents/Resources/reproxy\-mcp\-service install
.fi
.RE
.PP
Requests an agent sends are confined to the domain the original request
targeted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.reproxy/
All persistent state: settings, the HTTPS interception CA, saved
engagements, agent configuration and secrets.
.TP
.I ~/.reproxy/config.json
Settings, as edited in the Settings window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR launchctl (1)
